{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Johanan came to Mizpah with the commanders
He spoke of a plot that hung in the air
Baalis king of Ammon had [Bmaj7]sent a man
[G#m]Ishmael son of Nethaniah was [D#m]the danger
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He said strike him down before he strikes you
Scatter the Judeans who gather around
But Gedaliah refused to believe the [Bmaj7]news
[G#m]He said the words about Ishmael are not [D#m]true
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Baalis king of Ammon sent the blade
To kill the governor appointed by fate
The remnant of Judah is left [Bmaj7]to bleed
[G#m]While Ishmael son of Nethaniah leads the [D#m]deed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
In the seventh month they sat to eat
Ten men rose up with the sword at their feet
Gedaliah fell and the Chaldeans [Bmaj7]died
[G#m]The fighting men who stood by his [D#m]side
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Baalis king of Ammon sent the blade
To kill the governor appointed by fate
The remnant of Judah is left [Bmaj7]to bleed [G#m]
While Ishmael son of Netha[D#m]niah leads the deed
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [Bmaj7] | [G#m] |
